                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e239e49a-1435-382e-9c41-d8201eae4b08",
                        "entry_id": "46c2ede3-51f0-3daa-b8bb-2f1a1d3685e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Préjugé selon lequel tout le monde est cisgenre, qui privilégie par conséquent les identités cisgenres et néglige ou sous-représente les identités de genre non traditionnelles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Transféminisme"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a13b2138-71bc-4c4e-b491-e04916f25829",
                                "sense_id": "e239e49a-1435-382e-9c41-d8201eae4b08",
                                "text": "S’il existe sans aucun doute de la transphobie chez certain·e·s psys*, il s’agit la plupart du temps de cisnormativité. Autrement dit, des psys* cisgenres ont tendance à voir les autres à l’aune de leur propre vision du monde."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52f9d096-adbd-4a43-b5bd-9a8d09fccfe4",
                                "sense_id": "e239e49a-1435-382e-9c41-d8201eae4b08",
                                "text": "La cisnormativité engendre la marginalisation des personnes trans. Elle repose soit sur l’effacement de ces dernières, soit sur un préjugé favorable envers les personnes cisgenres, soit sur ces deux prémisses."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b523cb9b-d64d-41df-a35d-9681185f9a4b",
                        "source_entry_id": "46c2ede3-51f0-3daa-b8bb-2f1a1d3685e1",
                        "source_sense_id": "e239e49a-1435-382e-9c41-d8201eae4b08",
                        "target_lang_word": "cisnormativity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cisnormativity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bc4bdbd-f656-36a6-95ce-4df8ca3aa78d",
                                        "entry_id": "9b24d943-141b-3e24-9d8f-fab8743fc8bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The assumption that all human beings are cisgender, i.e. have a gender identity which matches their biological sex."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "neologism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c06ed3e5-b67c-49f4-9e80-d4dfbc0ae581",
                                                "sense_id": "9bc4bdbd-f656-36a6-95ce-4df8ca3aa78d",
                                                "text": "The erasure of transpeople's experiences can be understood, at least partially, as a function of the hegemony of cisnormativity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8436c24-8585-462c-9d4f-3ab4ae0fd3b3",
                                                "sense_id": "9bc4bdbd-f656-36a6-95ce-4df8ca3aa78d",
                                                "text": "These are the bodily consequences of cisnormativity—the prevalent and presumptuous assumption that cissexuality is the only acceptable and legible form of gender identity—which show us why, when we engage in feminist activism and inquiry, we must be trans-inclusive in our efforts to ensure that every human being deserves decency and justice when wronged."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
